        <div class="space-y-5 reveal" data-delay="200">
          <div class="bg-white border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-[0.95rem] mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-500">1.</span> Present-tense language for things that do not exist yet
            </h3>
            <p class="text-[0.9rem] text-bark-600 leading-relaxed">
              The Vision page says "BARK hires locally, buys locally" while the homepage CTA says "first cohort
              is forming." The Retreat Center describes guest experiences; the Incubator describes mentorship
              from experienced founders. None of these exist yet. BARK has no legal entity, no land, and no
              revenue. The Roadmap and Investors pages disclose this clearly, but other pages use present tense
              that could mislead casual readers.
            </p>
            <p class="text-[0.8rem] text-bark-400 mt-2">Affects: Homepage, Vision, Incubator, Retreat, Participate</p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-[0.95rem] mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-500">2.</span> Economic data that may be stale or volatile
            </h3>
            <p class="text-[0.9rem] text-bark-600 leading-relaxed">
              Bolivia's economy is changing rapidly. Foreign reserves (~$100M), inflation (20%+), credit rating
              (CCC-), and the dollar gap (70-115%) are all 2024-2025 snapshots that may be outdated by the time
              you read this. Coffee FOB pricing ($4.60/lb) and cost-of-living figures ($500-800/month) are also
              time-sensitive. The Gingery book set price ($50) is outdated &mdash; current price is $80-120.
            </p>
            <p class="text-[0.8rem] text-bark-400 mt-2">Affects: Resilience, Economy, Investors, Technopark</p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-[0.95rem] mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-500">3.</span> Scenario scoring methodology lacks disclosed weights
            </h3>
            <p class="text-[0.9rem] text-bark-600 leading-relaxed">
              The Scenarios page presents a 10-factor weighting model across 6 crisis scenarios with precise
              numerical scores (e.g., Bolivia 9.0 for Trust Crisis). The factors, weights, and scoring criteria
              are not disclosed, making the rankings impossible to verify or replicate. Self-generated scores
              are presented alongside externally sourced data, creating false equivalence between verified facts
              and internal ratings.
            </p>
            <p class="text-[0.8rem] text-bark-400 mt-2">Affects: Scenarios</p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-[0.95rem] mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-500">4.</span> WHO ranking from 2000 presented without date caveat
            </h3>
            <p class="text-[0.9rem] text-bark-600 leading-relaxed">
              The Resilience page cites Bolivia's WHO healthcare ranking as 126th of 190. This ranking is from
              the year 2000 and has not been updated by WHO since. Bolivia's healthcare system has changed
              significantly in 26 years. Readers may assume this is a current assessment.
            </p>
            <p class="text-[0.8rem] text-bark-400 mt-2">Affects: Resilience</p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-[0.95rem] mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-500">5.</span> Contradictions between pages
            </h3>
            <ul class="text-[0.9rem] text-bark-600 leading-relaxed space-y-2 mt-1">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-amber-500 shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
                <span>Family farms produce "~98%" (Resilience) vs "88%" (Scenarios) of food</span>
