        <p class="text-bark-600 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.85] mb-8 reveal" data-delay="100">
          We could not verify everything. The following data points are stated as estimates or
          qualified claims throughout the site because reliable primary sources do not exist
          or are not publicly accessible.
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-6 reveal" data-delay="200">
          <div class="bg-white border border-bark-200 rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-[0.95rem] mb-4">What We Could Not Verify</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-[0.9rem] text-bark-600 leading-relaxed">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="text-amber-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
                <span><strong>Coroico-specific crime statistics.</strong> Bolivia publishes national and departmental data, but no public municipal-level crime data exists for Nor Yungas province. Our safety assessment uses national and regional figures.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="text-amber-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
                <span><strong>Current internet speeds in Coroico.</strong> No public speed-test monitoring data for the area. Starlink availability is confirmed; actual user experience is anecdotal.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="text-amber-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
                <span><strong>Exact land prices.</strong> Bolivia has no public real-estate registry with transaction prices for the Coroico area. Pricing claims on the site are marked as estimates based on local inquiry.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="text-amber-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
                <span><strong>Hospital staffing levels.</strong> Coroico has a hospital, but staffing data (number of doctors, specialists, equipment) is not published online. The health page notes this gap.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="text-amber-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
                <span><strong>2024 census detailed results.</strong> Bolivia's most recent detailed census data at the municipal level dates from 2012. Updated population figures are extrapolated estimates.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="text-amber-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
                <span><strong>Intentional community failure rate.</strong> Widely cited ("most fail within five years") but the specific primary study is not easily traceable. We cite FIC research with a qualification.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="text-amber-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
                <span><strong>IDB $4.5B development package.</strong> Cited on Economy, Investors, and Network pages but no primary IDB source has been independently confirmed.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="text-amber-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
                <span><strong>Post-2025 political events.</strong> Claims about Bolivia's August 2025 election, US-Bolivia restored relations, and USAID closure are based on evolving political situations and may be stale.</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
